WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
- All right, let's close out
this hour with one last story

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.320
I hope will bring joy to your day.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.200
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.130
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.810
A Chicago artist got tired

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.150
of seeing potholes on the
streets of his neighborhood

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.970
so he came up with a
very creative solution,

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.050
mosaic arts.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.160
Super cool.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.350
Not only are mosaics long-lasting,

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.480
his works are truly beautiful.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.930
Now he fills the potholes around
the world with his tiling.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.480
Designing everything from animals to food,

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.100
to recreations of masterpieces

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.230
hanging at the Art Institute of Chicago.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.063
He's incredible.

00:00:32.063 --> 00:00:33.600
So we have him on the line right now.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.770
Let's say hi to Bachor

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.910
watching on NBC Chicago
at three, everybody.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:38.638
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.843
What's up, Bachor!?

00:00:39.843 --> 00:00:41.040
- Hey, Kelly.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.140
- You are super gifted, man.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.625
It's such a rad idea.

00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:46.290
How did you come up with the idea?

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.810
- Well, it all started with
an initial trip to Italy

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.630
back in the late 1990s.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:54.180
I kind of fell in love with ancient art

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.920
or ancient ruins and whatnot.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.510
And so when you do that,

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.370
you run across ancient mosaics.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.520
And ancient mosaics are
made with marble and glass

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.470
and marble and glass don't fade.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:09.240
So the art looks the way the
artist intended 2000 years ago.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.240
And so that thought to this
day kind of drives my artwork.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.880
So currently, I do fine art,

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.290
stuff that I sell on my website

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.670
and I do commissions and whatnot

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:24.390
but it was really the
pothole art that caught fire.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.568
And that was back in May of 2013.

00:01:26.568 --> 00:01:29.100
There were bad, bad potholes in Chicago

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.480
that particular year,

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.830
and especially on our street.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:35.430
And there was one stubborn
pothole in front of our house

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.420
that would get fixed

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.300
and then three months later
the asphalt will pop out

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.650
and they'd have to get
fixed again and whatnot.

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:44.220
And so I started thinking
the juxtaposition

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:47.370
of this art form I was so passionate about

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:48.990
that was so durable

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:53.130
with this unsolvable problem
outside of our house.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.770
And so what I decided to do one night,

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:56.603
and I did it at night

00:01:56.603 --> 00:01:58.230
because I wasn't sure
if it was legal or not,

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.240
is I went out there with some concrete

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.320
and a piece of mosaic art
and I fixed that pothole.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.630
And so what happened from there

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.030
is that it just kind of blew up.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.350
People love them.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.880
I ended up doing,

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.770
I've done over a hundred
now at this point.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.180
Most of them are in Chicago

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.010
but a lot of 'em are around the country.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:19.230
And there's even a couple international,

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:22.470
in like internationally
and like Finland and Italy.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.303
- That's so cool.

00:02:23.303 --> 00:02:25.230
And just helping your city look cooler.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.490
It's like you're not
just filling the pothole,

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:27.920
you're creating something beautiful too

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.250
in in the same moment.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.450
Thank you so much, Bachor.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.620
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.540
- [Bachor] Course, thank you.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:34.620
- And that's not all my man.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.990
Our season long partner
Pilot pen makers G2,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.610
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:40.590
want to honor truly unstoppable

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.060
and creative people just like you, sir.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.740
So, they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:44.700
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:45.533
How's that sound?

00:02:45.533 --> 00:02:46.366
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:47.199
- Whoa!

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:48.235
That's unexpected.

00:02:48.235 --> 00:02:49.068
Thank you.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.301
- [Kelly] Absolutely.
- [Bachor] That never happens.

00:02:50.301 --> 00:02:51.134
Thank you.

00:02:51.134 --> 00:02:51.967
- [Kelly] Thank you so much, Bachor.

00:02:51.967 --> 00:02:52.980
- [Bachor] Thank you so much.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.690
- Thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.630
Bryan Cranston, Rita
Wilson, Chef Kady Chen.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:58.463
Ya have a great day

00:02:58.463 --> 00:02:59.296
and if it's not,

00:02:59.296 --> 00:03:00.600
try and change it.

